- To summarize
    In a CNN, two small groups of pixels that overlap each other are compared mathematically to get a
    value. AI can use thousands of these small comparisons to identify individual parts of an image,
    then compare them to images in its corpus. From this, AI can put together an overall identification,
    without being overwhelmed.